{
  "tema": 5130,
  "slug": "estaba-gerundio-progresivo",
  "titulo": "Estaba + gerund",
  "subtitulo": "Estaba durmiendo cuando sonó el teléfono.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Estar in the imperfect + gerund (estaba comiendo) describes an action in progress at a moment in the past, often interrupted by another action in the preterite.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say what someone **was doing**, use **estar in the imperfect** + the **gerund**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "estaba / estabas / estaba / estábamos / estaban",
            "+ gerund (-ando / -iendo)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**estaba** trabajando"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**estabas** comiendo"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "**estaba** escribiendo"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "**estábamos** hablando"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "**estaban** durmiendo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Only **estar** changes; the gerund never does. Irregular gerunds stay irregular: **estaba leyendo**, **estaban durmiendo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It sets the background, and the **preterite** brings in the interruption: **Estaba durmiendo cuando sonó el teléfono.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It's close to the plain imperfect (**dormía**), but stresses that the action was **in the middle** of happening."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With **ir** and **venir**, Mexicans usually prefer the plain imperfect: **iba al trabajo** sounds more natural than **estaba yendo al trabajo**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Estaba durmiendo== cuando sonó el teléfono.",
              "en": "I was sleeping when the phone rang."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué ==estabas haciendo== a las diez?",
              "en": "What were you doing at ten?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Estábamos esperando== una ola cuando vimos un delfín.",
              "en": "We were waiting for a wave when we saw a dolphin."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi mamá ==estaba cocinando== frijoles.",
              "en": "My mom was cooking beans."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los niños ==estaban jugando== en el patio.",
              "en": "The kids were playing in the yard."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ustedes ==estaban viendo== la pelea?",
              "en": "Were you guys watching the fight?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Estaba leyendo== cuando se fue la luz.",
              "en": "I was reading when the power went out."
            },
            {
              "es": "Holden ==estaba hablando== con Naomi cuando sonó la alarma.",
              "en": "Holden was talking with Naomi when the alarm went off."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
